0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * ReBoot - Reboot into OS-9 or DECB
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *   1      ????/??/??  Alan DeKok
0000:                   * Started.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   ReBoot
0000:                            ttl   Reboot into OS-9 or DECB
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            endc
0000:                   
0011:                   tylg     set   Prgrm+Objct   
0080:                   atrv     set   ReEnt+Rev
0000:                   rev      set   $00
0000:                   
0000: 87CD04C8000D1180           mod   eom,name,tylg,atrv,start,size
0009: 0014E000
0000:                   
0000:                   *==================================================================
0000:                   * On boot-up, OS9p2 does (in order)
0000:                   * an I$ChDir to the directory specified in the Init file
0000:                   *     this opens an RBF buffer for the device, and at the minimum,
0000:                   *     allocates:
0000:                   * $0100 1 page by IOMan for the IRQ/VIRQ polling table
0000:                   * $0100 1 page by IOMan for the disk driver static storage
0000:                   * $0100 1 page by IOMan for the disk PD.BUF buffer
0000:                   * (the path descriptor comes out of memory allocated already by OS9p1
0000:                   *  from block 0)
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Next, OS9p2 does an I$Open to '/term' (or whatever, from the Init module)
0000:                   * $0100 1 page allocated for '/term' device static storage
0000:                   * $0100 1 page allocated for '/term' PD.BUF buffer
0000:                   *
0000:                   * VTIO does an F$Load to get GrfDrv into memory, and we then have
0000:                   * $0200 2 pages allocated by IOMan via F$AllPrc, for the F$Load
0000:                   *-------   total
0000:                   * $0700   pages UP from $4000, so GrfDrv can load
0000:                   
0000:                   *==================================================================
0000:                   * The system's memory map is set up as:
0000:                   * $0000-$1FFF: block 0, global system memory
0000:                   * $2000-$3FFF: this block MUST be free: grfdrv is loaded here on boot
0000:                   *              once booted, process descriptors, etc. get allocated here
0000:                   * $4000-$46FF: initial data storage for system prior to loading GrfDrv
0000:                   * $4700-$ECFF: OS9Boot file: $A600 maximum size
0000:                   * $ED00-$FEFF: kernel, and constant page at $FE00
0000:                   * $FF00-$FFFF: hardware, and RAM under block $3F that's unused by everyone!
0000:                   *==================================================================
0000:                   
A600:                   maxOS9Bt equ   $A600      max. size of the OS9Boot file
0000:                   
0000:                            org   0
0000:                   OS9Boot  rmb   maxOS9Bt
A600:                   Kernel   rmb   $1200        size of the kernel to use
B800:                   PrcDsc   rmb   $0200        current process descriptor
BA00:                   param.pt rmb   2            parameter pointer
BA02:                   os9btsz  rmb   2            size of the OS9Boot file
BA04:                   rbflag   rmb   2            -b -r flags
BA06:                   oflag    rmb   1            OS9Boot reload flag
BA07:                   kflag    rmb   1            kernel reload flag
BA08:                   gflag    rmb   1            GrfDrv reload flag
BA09:                   Param    rmb   $C000-.      shift everything up to $C000
C000:                   Stack    equ   .
C000:                   GrfDrv   rmb   $2000        so we now have all of the memory full
E000:                   SIZE     equ   .
E000:                   
E000:                   *==================================================================
E000:                   * We'll put all of the 'magic' code in GrfDrv's stack, which doesn't
E000:                   * care about being uninitialize
E000:                   *
E000:                   * Actually, this program puts it at offset $0000 in block $3F,
E000:                   * which is $E000 when the system is rebooted.  BOOT then copies
E000:                   * all of the information down to $1C80 before loading in the new OS9Boot
E000:                   * file, and copying the original BOOT module back to $ED00+$0130
E000:                   *==================================================================
E000:                            org   $1C80      where memory is ALWAYS mapped in
1C80:                   os9.siz  rmb   2          size of the os9boot file
1C82:                   grf.flg  rmb   1          flag: reload GrfDrv?
1C83:                   os9.dat  rmb   16         DAT image
1C93:                   boot     rmb   $01D0      original BOOT module
1E63:                   
000D: 5265426F6FF4      NAME     fcs   /ReBoot/
0013: 01                         fcb   $01
